// decimal_implicit_no_include.tk -- the IMPLICIT conversion of an integer to a
// `decimal` is a call into `lib/decimal.tk` (§ 6, `tk_dec_from_i64`), exactly
// as the explicit `(decimal) n` is, so a source that never included the file
// must be told which file it forgot and not be handed the core's own `call to
// unknown function` two phases later.
//
// The check lives in `tk_num_widen` (teko_typeof.tk), which is the one road
// all of D33's nine slots and `tk_ops_promote`'s mixed operand take, so this
// one fixture pins the wording for every one of them (D77, ruling 10). The
// explicit road's own fixture is `decimal_str_cast.tk`'s sibling: the message
// is `tk_prim_need_include`'s and is the same on both.
//
// expect-refuse: teko: decimal needs #include "decimal.tk" before it is used
// expect-refuse-line: 17

i64 main() {
    decimal d = 1;
    return 0;
}
